2026150,definition secondary trauma,msmarco_passage_28_2394291,DEFINITION of Boutonniere Deformity: It is a deformity of the fingers or toes in which the proximal inter-phalangeal joint is flexed and the distal inter-phalangeal joint is hyper-extended. It’s also called a central slip injury. A boutonnière deformity (BD) may develop either in the acute setting (secondary to trauma) or progressively (secondary to arthritis).,0,定义继发性创伤,定义继发性创伤. DEFINITION of Boutonniere Deformity: It is a deformity of the fingers or toes in which the proximal inter-phalangeal joint is flexed and the distal inter-phalangeal joint is hyper-extended. It’s also called a central slip injury. A boutonnière deformity (BD) may develop either in the acute setting (secondary to trauma) or progressively (secondary to arthritis).,2
